.TH WAVE-TRANSFER 1 "" "MacWave" "MacWave Manual"

.SH NAME
wave-transfer \- Rewrite the Mach-O references of already installed packages so they no longer name an absolute install path, then ad-hoc sign them again. Packages that are already position-independent are detected and skipped, so the command is safe to repeat. Dependencies used by the named packages are transferred too, otherwise the tree still could not be moved.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wave transfer <package>[@<version>] [, ...] | wave transfer \-\-all
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rewrite the Mach-O references of already installed packages so they no
longer name an absolute install path, then ad-hoc sign them again.
Packages that are already position-independent are detected and skipped,
so the command is safe to repeat. Dependencies used by the named
packages are transferred too, otherwise the tree still could not be
moved.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all
Transfer every installed package and dependency
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-dry\-run
Only report which packages would be transferred

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wave transfer jq
wave transfer ffmpeg@6.1
wave transfer jq, yq
wave transfer --all --dry-run
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
wave(1)
